Z||000017||Songman||04-10-2001||12:08 AM||||Personally, I have always loved these cars. I even loved the car that they copied.. the Stutz Blackhawk, built on Pontiac Grand Prix back in the 70s. If you have never seen once, go rent the movie Night Shift with Henry Winkler and Michael Keaton. Of course, in the movie they were pimps... but that is beside the point! The first one I ever saw of the Fiero Zimmer was pearl white.<P>Buy it Archie! I would if I could afford it!<P>Here's some Stutz pics...<BR>1972 Model<BR>For more pics go to: <A HREF="http://www.automaniacs.com/72Stutz" TARGET=_blank>http://www.automaniacs.com/72Stutz</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.automaniacs.com/72Stutz/72Stutz.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.automaniacs.com/72Stutz/smfront72Stutz.jpg"> <P>This one was Sammy Davis Jr's 72 Stutz...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.vegasauction.com/image/cars/1972%20stutz%20new.jpg"> <P>And this one was Evil Knievel's 74...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.vegasauction.com/image/cars/1974%20stutz%20evel.jpg"> <P>People have been building kits on Pontiacs for a long time!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||mrfixit58||04-10-2001||08:19 AM||||Keep in mind that this car was made during a time when chrome was still a major part of luxury car styling. The white one that was displayed in Daytona is owned by a member of my club so I've had the opportunity to look at this custom car very closely. It's absolutely the best fitting, best detailed rebody I've ever seen. Fit and finish are near perfect. Like it or not, it's got the heart of a Fiero underneath it's skin. Another vote for the versatility of our little car.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
